# TakeSample.srv
#
# The ROS2-service form of problog_project's TakeSample BT node (see
# module/contracts/schema.yaml's own TakeSample entry). A service, not
# an action, because it's INSTANTANEOUS -- a single fixed-probability
# coin flip, same "no Duration/Triggers, no continuous trajectory"
# shape as PlanPath.srv, not a durative walk like MoveTo.action/
# InstallTool.action/UninstallTool.action.
#
# success_probability (this problem's own config.yaml,
# sample.success_probability) is a ROS param on sample_service_node's
# own side, not a per-call argument -- same convention plan_service_node/
# condition_service_node already use for problog_frame_origin_x/y etc.

# This occurrence's own name (e.g. "soil1"), chosen by the tree author
# -- NOT the auto-generated ActionCode schema.yaml's own reason ports
# carry. A later SampleValueBelow/Equal/Over condition references this
# SAME id to check what value THIS specific sample came back with.
# sample_service_node.py also publishes it (with its drawn value, on
# success) on a latched topic so condition_service_node can answer
# those checks -- see that node's own module docstring.
string id
---
# One of "sample_success"/"sample_failure" -- matches
# problog_project/module/contracts/bt_actions.py's own bt_take_sample
# reference implementation's reason strings EXACTLY (a single
# random.random() < success_probability draw, no approximation).
string reason

# true iff reason is "sample_success".
bool status

# The drawn value, taken ONLY on success (matches schema.yaml's own
# sample_success(X,Y,V,SampleId,ActionCode) -- V is absent from
# sample_failure entirely), shaped ONE OF TWO WAYS by this problem's
# own config.yaml (sample_service_node's own value_discretized/
# value_mean/value_sigma params -- see problog_problem.sample_params):
#   - sample.value.discretized: an EXPLICIT {value,weight} outcome
#     list -- a weighted-random pick among exactly those values, which
#     need be neither integers nor within any particular range. Takes
#     priority if configured.
#   - sample.value.mean/sigma (default 5.0/2.0) -- the ORIGINAL
#     discretized Normal(mean,sigma) draw over the integers 0-10, used
#     whenever sample.value.discretized is absent.
# float64, not int32, so a discretized list's own arbitrary (non-
# integer, or out-of-0-10-range) values round-trip exactly -- the
# mean/sigma draw still always produces a whole number in [0,10] in
# that float64. Meaningless when status is false; sample_service_node.py
# always sets it to 0.0 in that case rather than leaving it at ROS's
# own implicit float64 default, so this is a documented "don't read
# it" rather than an indistinguishable one.
float64 value
